WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:04.237 line:0%
<i> Chile is a South American
 wilderness.</i>

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.774 line:0%
<i> Isolated from the rest
 of the continent,</i>

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:12.578 line:0%
<i> the country is a mosaic
 of different landscapes.</i>

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:18.617 line:0%
(music)

00:00:18.617 --> 00:00:23.789 line:0%
<i> None are quite as hostile
 as the Atacama Desert.</i>

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:26.726 line:0%
(music)

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:29.128 line:0%
<i> These are thirsty lands.</i>

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:34.100 line:0%
<i> Some areas haven't seen rain
 since history books began.</i>

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:37.269 line:0%
<i> It's the driest desert
 on Earth,</i>

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:43.275 line:0%
<i> where water has to be salvaged
 from unusual sources.</i>

00:00:43.275 --> 00:00:46.413 line:0%
<i> Risk is an everyday reality.</i>

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:53.419 line:0%
<i> Creatures in Chile's
 Atacama Desert adapt or die.</i>

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:58.591 line:0%
(music)

00:01:04.463 --> 00:01:06.532 line:0%
(music)

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:13.005 line:0%
(music)

00:01:13.005 --> 00:01:19.979 line:0%
(music)

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:25.985 line:0%
(music)

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:32.759 line:0%
(music)

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.598 line:0%
(music)

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:46.038 line:0%
(music)

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:52.077 line:0%
(music)

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:56.982 line:0%
<i> The Atacama is one of the most
 unforgiving places on Earth.</i>

00:01:56.982 --> 00:02:02.555 line:0%
(music)

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.957 line:0%
<i> Stretching across
 northern Chile,</i>

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:07.827 line:0%
<i> and straddling four countries,</i>

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:13.366 line:0%
<i> the Atacama Desert is
 almost as big as Cuba.</i>

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.301 line:0%
<i> Other than Earth's poles,</i>

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:20.439 line:0%
<i> no other place in the world
 is drier than here.</i>

00:02:20.439 --> 00:02:24.811 line:0%
<i> The wettest areas receive only
 half an inch of rain a year.</i>

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:28.948 line:0%
<i> But in the desert's center,</i>

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.384 line:0%
<i> as far as history knows,</i>

00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:34.320 line:0%
<i> it has never rained.</i>

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.290 line:0%
<i> Every corner of the compass
 reveals nothing but sand,</i>

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:40.993 line:0%
<i> stretching as far
 as the eye can see.</i>

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:46.865 line:0%
(music)

00:02:46.865 --> 00:02:50.803 line:0%
<i> It seems impossible that
 anything can live here.</i>

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:53.239 line:0%
(music)

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:59.045 line:0%
(music)

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:01.947 line:0%
<i> Despite the bleak
 prospects of life,</i>

00:03:01.947 --> 00:03:06.952 line:0%
<i> if you know how,
 there are ways of surviving.</i>

00:03:06.952 --> 00:03:12.457 line:0%
<i> The animals of the Atacama
 never overlook opportunity.</i>

00:03:12.457 --> 00:03:14.260 line:0%
<i> And when they find it,</i>

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:17.630 line:0%
<i> they fight to the death
 to defend it.</i>

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:22.335 line:0%
(music)

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:24.103 line:0%
<i> In the middle of the Atacama,</i>

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:28.307 line:0%
<i> life congregates around
 any source of water.</i>

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:33.812 line:0%
(music)

00:03:33.812 --> 00:03:39.185 line:0%
<i> The Salar de Atacama is
 the largest salt flat in Chile.</i>

00:03:41.253 --> 00:03:43.556 line:0%
<i> Its waters are filtered down
 from the Andes</i>

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:46.859 line:0%
<i> almost 200 miles to the east.</i>

00:03:48.794 --> 00:03:52.031 line:0%
<i> With no way to escape
 the mountain plateau,</i>

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:54.299 line:0%
<i> the waters are trapped.</i>

00:03:54.299 --> 00:03:56.669 line:0%
<i> They slowly evaporate,</i>

00:03:56.669 --> 00:04:01.274 line:0%
<i> leaving behind a vast expanse
 of thick salt crust.</i>

00:04:05.377 --> 00:04:10.617 line:0%
<i> It's here that the Atacama is
 host to a salt flat fighter.</i>

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:18.691 line:0%
<i> At the lake's edge,
 the Fabian's lizard is king.</i>

00:04:21.493 --> 00:04:25.197 line:0%
<i> There's not much to rule over,
 but whatever there is,</i>

00:04:25.197 --> 00:04:30.402 line:0%
<i> he'll defend with
 unrestrained ferocity.</i>

00:04:30.402 --> 00:04:33.339 line:0%
<i> And he doesn't do it alone.</i>

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:39.145 line:0%
<i> An unusual and
 ingenious lizard,</i>

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:44.683 line:0%
<i> he would be nothing
 without his partner in crime.</i>

00:04:44.683 --> 00:04:47.787 line:0%
<i> This female is his honey trap.</i>

00:04:50.422 --> 00:04:55.160 line:0%
<i> Her job is to distract invading
 males with sexual pheromones,</i>

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:59.432 line:0%
<i> allowing her mate to ambush
 the unsuspecting intruder.</i>

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:05.905 line:0%
<i> They use the highest salt crust
 as a look out.</i>

00:05:08.674 --> 00:05:10.943 line:0%
<i> From here they can
 survey their land</i>

00:05:10.943 --> 00:05:13.445 line:0%
<i> and spot any would-be usurpers.</i>

00:05:13.445 --> 00:05:18.350 line:0%
(music)

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:22.988 line:0%
<i> It isn't long before
 a trespasser catches their eye.</i>

00:05:22.988 --> 00:05:29.061 line:0%
(music)

00:05:29.061 --> 00:05:31.430 line:0%
<i> The scaly temptress
 wastes no time</i>

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:33.632 line:0%
<i> before flirting with the enemy.</i>

00:05:33.632 --> 00:05:39.071 line:0%
(music)

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:45.144 line:0%
(music)

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.880 line:0%
<i> He's enticed by her advances,</i>

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.250 line:0%
<i> but of course,
 it's too good to be true.</i>

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:56.021 line:0%
<i> Her partner spies on them
 from a distance,</i>

00:05:56.021 --> 00:05:58.558 line:0%
<i> waiting for the perfect moment.</i>

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:07.467 line:0%
<i> A signal from her,
 and he charges into battle.</i>

00:06:07.467 --> 00:06:12.138 line:0%
<i> He puffs himself out
 to intimidate his competitor,</i>

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:14.674 line:0%
<i> but his rival's no coward.</i>

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:20.179 line:0%
<i> The two salt flat fighters
 go for the kill.</i>

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:24.516 line:0%
(music)

00:06:24.516 --> 00:06:31.456 line:0%
(music)

00:06:31.456 --> 00:06:37.095 line:0%
(hissing)

00:06:37.095 --> 00:06:39.097 line:0%
<i> After countless throw downs,</i>

00:06:39.097 --> 00:06:42.434 line:0%
<i> the intruder is
 desperate to escape.</i>

00:06:42.434 --> 00:06:45.704 line:0%
<i> But this lizard's forte
 is fighting.</i>

00:06:45.704 --> 00:06:48.140 line:0%
(hissing)

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:53.012 line:0%
(music)

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:55.647 line:0%
(hiss)

00:06:55.647 --> 00:07:00.619 line:0%
(music)

00:07:00.619 --> 00:07:03.889 line:0%
<i> Finally, the intruder
 is allowed to leave,</i>

00:07:03.889 --> 00:07:06.292 line:0%
<i> a little battered and bruised.</i>

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:14.800 line:0%
<i> The couple have a good reason
 for defending this patch.</i>

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.301 line:0%
(buzzing)

00:07:16.301 --> 00:07:19.572 line:0%
<i> Their main source of food
 is swarming.</i>

00:07:19.572 --> 00:07:21.407 line:0%
<i> In the heat of the day,</i>

00:07:21.407 --> 00:07:25.144 line:0%
<i> black clouds of flies
 descend on the water's edge.</i>

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:32.184 line:0%
<i> For the lizards,
 catching them is an art form.</i>

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:34.553 line:0%
(music)

00:07:34.553 --> 00:07:39.458 line:0%
(music)

00:07:39.458 --> 00:07:43.896 line:0%
<i> But this isn't the case
 for everyone.</i>

00:07:43.896 --> 00:07:45.898 line:0%
<i> This Andean lapwing's methods</i>

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:48.400 line:0%
<i> are a little less
 sophisticated.</i>

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:54.773 line:0%
(music)

00:07:54.773 --> 00:08:00.879 line:0%
(music)

00:08:00.879 --> 00:08:03.281 line:0%
<i> There's little else to eat,</i>

00:08:03.281 --> 00:08:05.951 line:0%
<i> but there are plenty of flies
 to go around.</i>

00:08:05.951 --> 00:08:12.492 line:0%
(music)

00:08:17.229 --> 00:08:18.764 line:0%
<i> What little life exists here</i>

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:23.235 line:0%
<i> has been isolated
 for a long time.</i>

00:08:23.235 --> 00:08:27.640 line:0%
<i> It's had to adapt to the
 hostile climate of the Atacama.</i>

00:08:31.043 --> 00:08:33.645 line:0%
<i> The waters here have
 a similar salt concentration</i>

00:08:33.645 --> 00:08:35.781 line:0%
<i> to the Dead Sea.</i>

00:08:35.781 --> 00:08:39.451 line:0%
<i> Too high to sustain much,
 but what there is</i>

00:08:39.451 --> 00:08:43.889 line:0%
<i> entices the desert's
 most flamboyant residents.</i>

00:08:43.889 --> 00:08:46.391 line:0%
(squawking)

00:08:46.391 --> 00:08:49.261 line:0%
<i> Flamingoes.</i>

00:08:49.261 --> 00:08:52.964 line:0%
(squawking)

00:08:52.964 --> 00:08:55.234 line:0%
<i> These birds wear pink,</i>

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:59.171 line:0%
<i> but they're no
 delicate dancers.</i>

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:01.006 line:0%
<i> Everything about them
 is tailored</i>

00:09:01.006 --> 00:09:04.343 line:0%
<i> to counter
 the punishing conditions.</i>

00:09:04.343 --> 00:09:07.713 line:0%
<i> They've spent 30 million years
 biologically evolving</i>

00:09:07.713 --> 00:09:11.116 line:0%
<i> to the demands of life.</i>

00:09:11.116 --> 00:09:16.388 line:0%
<i> They're specially adapted
 to these brackish waters.</i>

00:09:16.388 --> 00:09:19.225 line:0%
<i> Flamingoes are one
 of the few animals on Earth</i>

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:21.660 line:0%
<i> that are able
 to drink the water.</i>

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:27.700 line:0%
(music)

00:09:27.700 --> 00:09:29.669 line:0%
<i> Just because
 they can cope here</i>

00:09:29.669 --> 00:09:33.639 line:0%
<i> doesn't mean that life's easy
 for Chile's flamingoes.</i>

00:09:36.875 --> 00:09:38.477 line:0%
<i> In the early afternoon heat</i>

00:09:38.477 --> 00:09:41.881 line:0%
<i> the air in the Atacama
 grows restless.</i>

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.753 line:0%
<i> The rising temperatures
 create dust devils</i>

00:09:47.753 --> 00:09:50.189 line:0%
<i> that churn their way
 across the landscape</i>

00:09:50.189 --> 00:09:54.026 line:0%
<i> at speeds of
 up to 45 miles per hour.</i>

00:09:56.862 --> 00:10:00.532 line:0%
<i> A reminder of just how
 unwelcome life is</i>

00:10:00.532 --> 00:10:02.802 line:0%
<i> in the Atacama Desert.</i>

00:10:12.944 --> 00:10:14.947 line:0%
<i> The conditions
 of the Atacama Desert</i>

00:10:14.947 --> 00:10:17.182 line:0%
<i> are more similar
 to the surface of Mars</i>

00:10:17.182 --> 00:10:19.986 line:0%
<i> than anywhere else on Earth.</i>

00:10:23.989 --> 00:10:26.258 line:0%
<i> So much so,
 that NASA comes here</i>

00:10:26.258 --> 00:10:29.762 line:0%
<i> to help unlock the secrets
 of the Red Planet.</i>

00:10:33.265 --> 00:10:35.767 line:0%
<i> This desert is
 50 times more arid</i>

00:10:35.767 --> 00:10:39.871 line:0%
<i> than California's Death Valley.</i>

00:10:39.871 --> 00:10:42.974 line:0%
<i> As well as being the driest
 desert in the world,</i>

00:10:42.974 --> 00:10:48.647 line:0%
<i> the Atacama is also
 one of the oldest.</i>

00:10:48.647 --> 00:10:52.952 line:0%
<i> It hasn't changed much
 in 150 million years.</i>

00:10:55.987 --> 00:10:58.557 line:0%
<i> Bacteria in the soils
 of the Atacama</i>

00:10:58.557 --> 00:11:02.594 line:0%
<i> could hold the key to the
 beginning of planetary life.</i>

00:11:02.594 --> 00:11:05.063 line:0%
(music)

00:11:05.063 --> 00:11:10.036 line:0%
(music)

00:11:12.003 --> 00:11:13.505 line:0%
<i> In the middle of the desert</i>

00:11:13.505 --> 00:11:15.140 line:0%
<i> this lagoon is home</i>

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:19.878 line:0%
<i> to one of the oldest forms
 of life on Earth.</i>

00:11:19.878 --> 00:11:23.616 line:0%
(music)

00:11:23.616 --> 00:11:25.985 line:0%
<i> These stromatolite structures</i>

00:11:25.985 --> 00:11:32.491 line:0%
<i> are made from layer upon layer
 of very simple bacteria.</i>

00:11:32.491 --> 00:11:34.192 line:0%
<i> Life on Earth as we know it</i>

00:11:34.192 --> 00:11:38.397 line:0%
<i> owes its existence
 to these modest-looking lumps.</i>

00:11:38.397 --> 00:11:44.970 line:0%
(music)

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:48.039 line:0%
<i> It's this bacteria that
 first introduced oxygen</i>

00:11:48.039 --> 00:11:50.943 line:0%
<i> into the planet's atmosphere</i>

00:11:50.943 --> 00:11:56.081 line:0%
<i> allowing life on Earth
 to explode.</i>

00:11:56.081 --> 00:11:57.850 line:0%
<i> The waters of the lagoon</i>

00:11:57.850 --> 00:12:01.487 line:0%
<i> reveal more of the world's
 ancient life-forms.</i>

00:12:03.889 --> 00:12:05.691 line:0%
<i> Triops.</i>

00:12:08.226 --> 00:12:11.530 line:0%
<i> These little creatures are one
 of the oldest animal species</i>

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:13.131 line:0%
<i> still in existence.</i>

00:12:13.131 --> 00:12:16.535 line:0%
<i> Unchanged for more than
 70 million years.</i>

00:12:19.371 --> 00:12:21.072 line:0%
<i> They're born survivors,</i>

00:12:21.072 --> 00:12:24.910 line:0%
<i> able to withstand
 very warm alkaline waters.</i>

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:30.116 line:0%
(music)

00:12:32.117 --> 00:12:34.119 line:0%
<i> Today, these skills are evident</i>

00:12:34.119 --> 00:12:37.823 line:0%
<i> in the Atacama's
 other inhabitants.</i>

00:12:37.823 --> 00:12:40.492 line:0%
<i> More than merely
 salt lake experts,</i>

00:12:40.492 --> 00:12:43.361 line:0%
<i> flamingoes are one of the few
 animals able to withstand</i>

00:12:43.361 --> 00:12:47.767 line:0%
<i> the caustic soda found
 in the desert's thermal pools.</i>

00:12:57.809 --> 00:13:04.316 line:0%
<i> Chile is home to more than
 300 geothermal fields.</i>

00:13:04.316 --> 00:13:07.886 line:0%
<i> Spots where heat from deep
 within the molten earth</i>

00:13:07.886 --> 00:13:10.622 line:0%
<i> can be felt on the surface.</i>

00:13:10.622 --> 00:13:14.493 line:0%
<i> Most of them can be found
 in the Atacama.</i>

00:13:14.493 --> 00:13:17.729 line:0%
<i> Some are more noticeable
 than others.</i>

00:13:17.729 --> 00:13:20.198 line:0%
(music)

00:13:20.198 --> 00:13:26.771 line:0%
(music)

00:13:26.771 --> 00:13:32.811 line:0%
(music)

00:13:32.811 --> 00:13:38.817 line:0%
(music)

00:13:38.817 --> 00:13:43.655 line:0%
<i> More than 80 geysers are dotted
 throughout the desert.</i>

00:13:43.655 --> 00:13:48.260 line:0%
<i> Chile's most famous are
 the El Tatio geysers.</i>

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.061 line:0%
<i> It's the biggest
 cluster of geysers</i>

00:13:50.061 --> 00:13:52.063 line:0%
<i> in the Southern Hemisphere,</i>

00:13:52.063 --> 00:13:55.968 line:0%
<i> and the third largest on Earth.</i>

00:13:55.968 --> 00:13:59.438 line:0%
<i> Located 14,000 feet
 above sea level,</i>

00:13:59.438 --> 00:14:03.408 line:0%
<i> they belong to the highest
 geothermal field in the world.</i>

00:14:03.408 --> 00:14:09.314 line:0%
(music)

00:14:09.314 --> 00:14:13.018 line:0%
<i> At these altitudes, water is
 a little easier to come by</i>

00:14:13.018 --> 00:14:16.155 line:0%
<i> than in the desert's
 heartlands.</i>

00:14:16.155 --> 00:14:17.922 line:0%
<i> Snowmelt from
 the nearby mountains</i>

00:14:17.922 --> 00:14:23.294 line:0%
<i> collects and forms small lakes
 on the Altiplano.</i>

00:14:23.294 --> 00:14:25.997 line:0%
<i> At this altitude
 there are strange creatures</i>

00:14:25.997 --> 00:14:28.567 line:0%
<i> that call the water pools home.</i>

00:14:31.603 --> 00:14:35.206 line:0%
<i> The giant coot
 lives up to its name.</i>

00:14:35.206 --> 00:14:38.410 line:0%
<i> This water bird
 weighs five pounds.</i>

00:14:38.410 --> 00:14:42.448 line:0%
(music)

00:14:42.448 --> 00:14:46.184 line:0%
<i> Huge feet allow them to carry
 their bulk over floating weeds</i>

00:14:46.184 --> 00:14:48.287 line:0%
<i> without sinking.</i>

00:14:52.323 --> 00:14:55.594 line:0%
<i> This male is looking
 for building material.</i>

00:14:57.529 --> 00:15:01.967 line:0%
<i> Giant coots are house proud.</i>

00:15:01.967 --> 00:15:08.339 line:0%
<i> Their entire day is dedicated
 to constructing their nest.</i>

00:15:08.339 --> 00:15:10.341 line:0%
<i> They work together
 with their partners,</i>

00:15:10.341 --> 00:15:12.911 line:0%
<i> spending hours adding
 to the structure</i>

00:15:12.911 --> 00:15:15.581 line:0%
<i> with plants they've torn up
 from the lakebed.</i>

00:15:15.581 --> 00:15:18.950 line:0%
(squawking)

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:24.389 line:0%
(music)

00:15:24.389 --> 00:15:30.528 line:0%
(music)

00:15:30.528 --> 00:15:37.236 line:0%
(music)

00:15:37.236 --> 00:15:40.172 line:0%
<i> There's a lot at stake
 for these homeowners.</i>

00:15:46.311 --> 00:15:49.381 line:0%
<i> Trespassing isn't tolerated.</i>

00:15:52.684 --> 00:15:55.287 line:0%
<i> Yet some coots aren't willing
 to put in the time</i>

00:15:55.287 --> 00:15:58.323 line:0%
<i> to do their own
 home improvements.</i>

00:15:58.323 --> 00:16:03.228 line:0%
(music)

00:16:03.228 --> 00:16:09.668 line:0%
(music)

00:16:09.668 --> 00:16:15.674 line:0%
(music)

00:16:15.674 --> 00:16:19.210 line:0%
<i> Nest-looting in this
 neighborhood is rife.</i>

00:16:19.210 --> 00:16:24.383 line:0%
(music)

00:16:28.153 --> 00:16:29.788 line:0%
<i> Enough's enough.</i>

00:16:29.788 --> 00:16:33.458 line:0%
<i> This coot isn't having it.</i>

00:16:33.458 --> 00:16:35.727 line:0%
<i> He sets his sights
 on the latest thief</i>

00:16:35.727 --> 00:16:39.498 line:0%
<i> and charges after him.</i>

00:16:39.498 --> 00:16:41.633 line:0%
<i> Giant coots can't really fly.</i>

00:16:41.633 --> 00:16:43.902 line:0%
<i> But their incredibly
 powerful legs</i>

00:16:43.902 --> 00:16:45.670 line:0%
<i> and huge crab-like feet</i>

00:16:45.670 --> 00:16:48.673 line:0%
<i> allow them to blaze
 through the water.</i>

00:16:48.673 --> 00:16:52.711 line:0%
(music)

00:16:52.711 --> 00:16:58.016 line:0%
(squawking)

00:16:58.016 --> 00:17:00.452 line:0%
<i> When the homeowner
 catches up with the thief,</i>

00:17:00.452 --> 00:17:06.491 line:0%
<i> he initiates the coot version
 of kickboxing.</i>

00:17:06.491 --> 00:17:09.394 line:0%
(music)

00:17:09.394 --> 00:17:16.034 line:0%
(music)

00:17:16.034 --> 00:17:17.702 line:0%
<i> Though this might look silly,</i>

00:17:17.702 --> 00:17:20.572 line:0%
<i> there's a lot of power
 behind each slap.</i>

00:17:20.572 --> 00:17:22.674 line:0%
<i> The claws on the end
 of the coots' feet</i>

00:17:22.674 --> 00:17:25.644 line:0%
<i> are incredibly sharp.</i>

00:17:25.644 --> 00:17:27.546 line:0%
<i> In the chaos of the fight,</i>

00:17:27.546 --> 00:17:31.383 line:0%
<i> they've trespassed onto
 another neighbor's territory.</i>

00:17:31.383 --> 00:17:35.153 line:0%
(music)

00:17:35.153 --> 00:17:39.057 line:0%
<i> The fight has now escalated
 into a brawl.</i>

00:17:39.057 --> 00:17:45.997 line:0%
(music)

00:17:45.997 --> 00:17:52.738 line:0%
(music)

00:17:52.738 --> 00:17:57.575 line:0%
(squawking)

00:17:57.575 --> 00:18:03.081 line:0%
(music)

00:18:03.081 --> 00:18:09.488 line:0%
(music)

00:18:09.488 --> 00:18:13.125 line:0%
<i> Finally, exhausted,
 everyone cools off.</i>

00:18:16.828 --> 00:18:19.398 line:0%
(shrieking)

00:18:19.398 --> 00:18:21.800 line:0%
<i> But the peace will definitely
 be short-lived</i>

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:24.136 line:0%
<i> with tempers like these.</i>

00:18:33.344 --> 00:18:36.982 line:0%
<i> As the sun sets,
 shadows in Chile's Altiplano</i>

00:18:36.982 --> 00:18:40.252 line:0%
<i> stretch their way up
 the banks of the Andes.</i>

00:18:43.588 --> 00:18:47.825 line:0%
<i> Meanwhile in the desert's
 dry and dusty interior,</i>

00:18:47.825 --> 00:18:51.563 line:0%
<i> an unlikely animal
 remains wide awake.</i>

00:19:00.839 --> 00:19:02.573 line:0%
<i> In the middle of Chile's
 Atacama Desert,</i>

00:19:02.573 --> 00:19:06.145 line:0%
<i> the skies are clear
 nearly 24 hours a day.</i>

00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:10.248 line:0%
<i> Even clouds don't venture</i>

00:19:10.248 --> 00:19:15.587 line:0%
<i> into the seemingly
 desolate wasteland.</i>

00:19:15.587 --> 00:19:17.689 line:0%
<i> And because of their absence,</i>

00:19:17.689 --> 00:19:21.193 line:0%
<i> temperatures at night
 are near freezing.</i>

00:19:23.595 --> 00:19:25.663 line:0%
<i> It's now that
 one of the Atacama's</i>

00:19:25.663 --> 00:19:27.732 line:0%
<i> most surprising inhabitants</i>

00:19:27.732 --> 00:19:29.901 line:0%
<i> must draw on some
 serious fortitude</i>

00:19:29.901 --> 00:19:32.437 line:0%
<i> to get through the night.</i>

00:19:34.305 --> 00:19:39.211 line:0%
(peeping)

00:19:39.211 --> 00:19:42.447 line:0%
<i> The gray gull nests here
 in the desert.</i>

00:19:42.447 --> 00:19:43.915 line:0%
(squawk)

00:19:43.915 --> 00:19:49.287 line:0%
<i> Make no mistake,
 these are seabirds.</i>

00:19:49.287 --> 00:19:50.956 line:0%
<i> For years no one knew</i>

00:19:50.956 --> 00:19:54.592 line:0%
<i> where these seemingly ordinary
 birds went to nest.</i>

00:19:54.592 --> 00:19:58.263 line:0%
<i> Then they were stumbled upon
 in 1945,</i>

00:19:58.263 --> 00:20:01.299 line:0%
<i> here in the driest desert
 in the world.</i>

00:20:01.299 --> 00:20:03.368 line:0%
(peeping)

00:20:03.368 --> 00:20:05.904 line:0%
<i> But these gulls aren't lost.</i>

00:20:05.904 --> 00:20:08.072 line:0%
<i> This is actually
 a perfect example</i>

00:20:08.072 --> 00:20:12.944 line:0%
<i> of the ingenuity
 of the Atacama's animals.</i>

00:20:12.944 --> 00:20:16.214 line:0%
<i> They could be here because
 there are barely any predators.</i>

00:20:16.214 --> 00:20:22.287 line:0%
<i> In that sense, it's the perfect
 spot to raise a family.</i>

00:20:22.287 --> 00:20:26.158 line:0%
<i> But that perk comes
 with several catches.</i>

00:20:26.158 --> 00:20:29.428 line:0%
<i> The parents must take turns
 traveling more than 60 miles</i>

00:20:29.428 --> 00:20:33.765 line:0%
<i> to the coast to collect food
 and water for their chicks.</i>

00:20:38.102 --> 00:20:42.941 line:0%
<i> Daytime brings
 even more challenges.</i>

00:20:42.941 --> 00:20:44.576 line:0%
<i> As the temperature rises,</i>

00:20:44.576 --> 00:20:49.247 line:0%
<i> these eggs could cook
 in the baking hot soils.</i>

00:20:49.247 --> 00:20:50.948 line:0%
<i> In the hottest part of the day,</i>

00:20:50.948 --> 00:20:53.918 line:0%
<i> the parent on duty
 must stand over the eggs,</i>

00:20:53.918 --> 00:20:58.289 line:0%
<i> keeping them in the shade.</i>

00:20:58.289 --> 00:21:01.860 line:0%
<i> It's a selfless act
 in these temperatures.</i>

00:21:06.164 --> 00:21:08.933 line:0%
<i> But the gulls are
 well adjusted to life here.</i>

00:21:08.933 --> 00:21:10.202 line:0%
<i> The colors of their feathers</i>

00:21:10.202 --> 00:21:12.370 line:0%
<i> are thought to be
 an adaptation,</i>

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:15.073 line:0%
<i> enabling them to radiate heat.</i>

00:21:15.073 --> 00:21:18.510 line:0%
<i> Even the eggs are well designed
 for the desert.</i>

00:21:21.846 --> 00:21:23.815 line:0%
<i> Their hard, impervious shell</i>

00:21:23.815 --> 00:21:28.820 line:0%
<i> means little moisture
 evaporates from inside the egg.</i>

00:21:28.820 --> 00:21:34.258 line:0%
<i> In fact, 30% less than some
 other desert nesting birds.</i>

00:21:34.258 --> 00:21:36.862 line:0%
(peeping)

00:21:40.198 --> 00:21:42.600 line:0%
(squawk)

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:44.536 line:0%
(peeping)

00:21:44.536 --> 00:21:46.171 line:0%
<i> When they're old enough,</i>

00:21:46.171 --> 00:21:49.006 line:0%
<i> the chicks take turns
 giving each other shade.</i>

00:21:49.006 --> 00:21:54.346 line:0%
(peeping)

00:21:54.346 --> 00:21:57.849 line:0%
<i> But mom always makes
 a better sunshield.</i>

00:22:00.986 --> 00:22:06.391 line:0%
<i> Some don't survive
 this perilous start to life.</i>

00:22:06.391 --> 00:22:08.360 line:0%
<i> But those that do
 won't wait long</i>

00:22:08.360 --> 00:22:12.196 line:0%
<i> before making their first
 pilgrimage to the shore.</i>

00:22:12.196 --> 00:22:17.769 line:0%
(music)

00:22:17.769 --> 00:22:22.039 line:0%
<i> After around 40 days
 and 40 nights in the desert,</i>

00:22:22.039 --> 00:22:24.242 line:0%
<i> gray gull chicks finally fledge</i>

00:22:24.242 --> 00:22:28.713 line:0%
<i> and follow their parents
 to the ocean.</i>

00:22:28.713 --> 00:22:32.484 line:0%
<i> The eastern edge of the Pacific
 awaits them.</i>

00:22:34.786 --> 00:22:36.888 line:0%
(music)

00:22:36.888 --> 00:22:43.428 line:0%
(music)

00:22:43.428 --> 00:22:46.331 line:0%
<i> At the midway mark
 of the Atacama's coastline,</i>

00:22:46.331 --> 00:22:50.468 line:0%
<i> the desert is littered
 with boulders and rocks.</i>

00:22:50.468 --> 00:22:56.908 line:0%
(music)

00:22:56.908 --> 00:23:01.646 line:0%
<i> Here the sea batters the shore
 with furious waves,</i>

00:23:01.646 --> 00:23:04.916 line:0%
<i> often 25 feet tall.</i>

00:23:04.916 --> 00:23:09.887 line:0%
(music)

00:23:09.887 --> 00:23:13.558 line:0%
<i> Despite the odds,
 it's on this turbulent border</i>

00:23:13.558 --> 00:23:15.827 line:0%
<i> that the Atacama Pacific iguana</i>

00:23:15.827 --> 00:23:18.997 line:0%
<i> has made a successful
 enterprise.</i>

00:23:24.769 --> 00:23:26.571 line:0%
<i> Like its name suggests,</i>

00:23:26.571 --> 00:23:31.143 line:0%
<i> this lizard bridges the gap
 between desert and ocean.</i>

00:23:33.210 --> 00:23:37.349 line:0%
<i> They're another of
 the Atacama's unusual lizards.</i>

00:23:39.417 --> 00:23:46.024 line:0%
<i> But like all reptiles, they're
 pretty lazy in the morning.</i>

00:23:46.024 --> 00:23:48.293 line:0%
<i> They begin the day
 with a bit of sunbathing</i>

00:23:48.293 --> 00:23:50.728 line:0%
<i> to raise their metabolism.</i>

00:23:50.728 --> 00:23:57.335 line:0%
(music)

00:23:57.335 --> 00:24:01.239 line:0%
<i> They need all the energy they
 can get for what's in store.</i>

00:24:08.713 --> 00:24:11.649 line:0%
<i> As the sun rises
 and low tide approaches,</i>

00:24:11.649 --> 00:24:14.852 line:0%
<i> Pacific lizards begin
 checking the ocean.</i>

00:24:14.852 --> 00:24:21.526 line:0%
(music)

00:24:21.526 --> 00:24:27.965 line:0%
(music)

00:24:27.965 --> 00:24:32.537 line:0%
<i> Climbing to a higher point,
 they can survey the water.</i>

00:24:35.273 --> 00:24:38.142 line:0%
<i> They're not here
 out of curiosity.</i>

00:24:38.142 --> 00:24:41.579 line:0%
(music)

00:24:41.579 --> 00:24:47.885 line:0%
(music)

00:24:47.885 --> 00:24:51.490 line:0%
<i> They know all too well
 what the water can do.</i>

00:24:55.393 --> 00:24:57.996 line:0%
<i> These lizards are not
 built for swimming,</i>

00:24:57.996 --> 00:25:01.333 line:0%
<i> and they stand no chance
 in these waves.</i>

00:25:05.804 --> 00:25:10.275 line:0%
<i> That's why what they do next
 is so surprising.</i>

00:25:10.275 --> 00:25:13.678 line:0%
<i> These rocks are covered
 in nutrient-rich algae,</i>

00:25:13.678 --> 00:25:16.848 line:0%
<i> a veritable feast in this area.</i>

00:25:16.848 --> 00:25:23.554 line:0%
(music)

00:25:23.554 --> 00:25:28.926 line:0%
(music)

00:25:28.926 --> 00:25:31.363 line:0%
<i> Timing is everything.</i>

00:25:34.432 --> 00:25:41.306 line:0%
<i> The lizards risk life and limb
 to reach the precious food.</i>

00:25:41.306 --> 00:25:43.008 line:0%
<i> Eating as much as they can</i>

00:25:43.008 --> 00:25:45.610 line:0%
<i> before scuttling
 back to safety.</i>

00:25:54.785 --> 00:25:57.221 line:0%
(music)

00:25:57.221 --> 00:26:02.393 line:0%
(music)

00:26:02.393 --> 00:26:05.196 line:0%
<i> Not only could
 they be swept away,</i>

00:26:05.196 --> 00:26:08.265 line:0%
<i> but the cold waters mean the
 lizard loses a lot of energy</i>

00:26:08.265 --> 00:26:10.134 line:0%
<i> retrieving a meal.</i>

00:26:10.134 --> 00:26:12.570 line:0%
(music)

00:26:12.570 --> 00:26:19.143 line:0%
(music)

00:26:19.143 --> 00:26:24.815 line:0%
(music)

00:26:24.815 --> 00:26:29.120 line:0%
(music)

00:26:31.790 --> 00:26:34.392 line:0%
<i> Each trip has to be countered</i>

00:26:34.392 --> 00:26:38.730 line:0%
<i> with moments of rest
 in the sun.</i>

00:26:38.730 --> 00:26:43.301 line:0%
<i> But it's a fair trade-off
 for food that can't run away.</i>

00:26:57.515 --> 00:27:01.219 line:0%
<i> The waters on the coast
 of Chile are especially icy;</i>

00:27:01.219 --> 00:27:04.055 line:0%
<i> they come from a polar ocean.</i>

00:27:04.055 --> 00:27:08.459 line:0%
(music)

00:27:08.459 --> 00:27:10.962 line:0%
<i> The Humboldt Current is
 several degrees colder</i>

00:27:10.962 --> 00:27:15.566 line:0%
<i> than the rest of the Pacific.</i>

00:27:15.566 --> 00:27:18.736 line:0%
<i> Strong winds drive this
 slow, cold stream of water</i>

00:27:18.736 --> 00:27:23.808 line:0%
<i> up the western edge of Chile
 from Antarctica.</i>

00:27:23.808 --> 00:27:26.477 line:0%
<i> The Humboldt reaches
 600 miles wide</i>

00:27:26.477 --> 00:27:29.381 line:0%
<i> and is as deep as the seafloor.</i>

00:27:31.816 --> 00:27:35.219 line:0%
<i> The cold-water upwelling brings
 with it nutrient-rich debris</i>

00:27:35.219 --> 00:27:39.891 line:0%
<i> from the seabed,
 which phytoplankton thrive on.</i>

00:27:41.726 --> 00:27:45.096 line:0%
<i> And in turn, hundreds of
 ocean animals come to feast</i>

00:27:45.096 --> 00:27:48.299 line:0%
<i> on the riches
 of Chile's coastline.</i>

00:27:48.299 --> 00:27:50.735 line:0%
(music)

00:27:50.735 --> 00:27:55.606 line:0%
(music)

00:27:55.606 --> 00:27:58.642 line:0%
<i> With such an abundance
 of water and food,</i>

00:27:58.642 --> 00:28:00.678 line:0%
<i> the Humboldt seems
 to have nothing in common</i>

00:28:00.678 --> 00:28:05.116 line:0%
<i> with the desert
 that runs alongside it.</i>

00:28:05.116 --> 00:28:09.921 line:0%
<i> But in fact, this current is
 what makes the Atacama so dry.</i>

00:28:13.557 --> 00:28:17.962 line:0%
(music)

00:28:17.962 --> 00:28:19.564 line:0%
<i> The cold air above the Humboldt</i>

00:28:19.564 --> 00:28:23.401 line:0%
<i> acts as a vacuum
 for airborne moisture.</i>

00:28:23.401 --> 00:28:29.407 line:0%
(music)

00:28:29.407 --> 00:28:34.045 line:0%
<i> Fog and mists hover as banks of
 cloud over Chile's shoreline...</i>

00:28:36.681 --> 00:28:39.150 line:0%
<i> trapped by a collision
 of air pressure.</i>

00:28:39.150 --> 00:28:45.189 line:0%
(music)

00:28:45.189 --> 00:28:47.592 line:0%
<i> But for a few hours every day,</i>

00:28:47.592 --> 00:28:50.861 line:0%
<i> warmer temperatures
 release the fog,</i>

00:28:50.861 --> 00:28:55.033 line:0%
<i> and it moves up the cliffs
 toward the desert,</i>

00:28:55.033 --> 00:28:59.303 line:0%
<i> warming into the edge
 of the Atacama.</i>

00:28:59.303 --> 00:29:04.408 line:0%
<i> This is known
 as the camanchaca.</i>

00:29:04.408 --> 00:29:08.345 line:0%
<i> Strong winds accompany
 this fog phenomenon.</i>

00:29:08.345 --> 00:29:12.417 line:0%
(music)

00:29:12.417 --> 00:29:16.187 line:0%
<i> The desert is encased
 in seconds.</i>

00:29:19.157 --> 00:29:21.692 line:0%
<i> For a few hours
 nearly every day,</i>

00:29:21.692 --> 00:29:23.260 line:0%
<i> the fringes of the Atacama</i>

00:29:23.260 --> 00:29:28.499 line:0%
<i> are drenched in
 fine water droplets.</i>

00:29:28.499 --> 00:29:33.871 line:0%
<i> It's a lifeline for animals and
 plants on the edge of survival.</i>

00:29:33.871 --> 00:29:37.809 line:0%
<i> Here cactus flourish
 in the path of the mists.</i>

00:29:40.611 --> 00:29:44.115 line:0%
<i> And are even covered
 in water-loving lichen.</i>

00:29:44.115 --> 00:29:49.387 line:0%
(music)

00:29:49.387 --> 00:29:53.657 line:0%
<i> An oasis for
 the Atacama's animals.</i>

00:29:53.657 --> 00:30:00.264 line:0%
(music)

00:30:00.264 --> 00:30:04.469 line:0%
<i> But the fog will last
 only an hour or two,</i>

00:30:04.469 --> 00:30:08.806 line:0%
<i> so they must seize
 the opportunity while it lasts.</i>

00:30:08.806 --> 00:30:12.176 line:0%
(chirping)

00:30:12.176 --> 00:30:17.649 line:0%
(chirping)

00:30:23.588 --> 00:30:26.457 line:0%
<i> The camanchaca entices
 a surprising creature</i>

00:30:26.457 --> 00:30:28.092 line:0%
<i> out of hiding.</i>

00:30:32.630 --> 00:30:34.332 line:0%
<i> Hummingbirds are
 usually only found</i>

00:30:34.332 --> 00:30:37.435 line:0%
<i> among forests and flowers.</i>

00:30:37.435 --> 00:30:41.138 line:0%
<i> But the daily fog makes life on
 the edge of the desert possible</i>

00:30:41.138 --> 00:30:44.275 line:0%
<i> for the oasis hummingbird.</i>

00:30:44.275 --> 00:30:45.943 line:0%
<i> On Chile's coastline,</i>

00:30:45.943 --> 00:30:49.848 line:0%
<i> they capitalize on the riches
 of the camanchaca.</i>

00:30:52.316 --> 00:30:54.852 line:0%
<i> Their long bills allow them
 to extract nectar</i>

00:30:54.852 --> 00:30:59.390 line:0%
<i> from the flowering cacti.</i>

00:30:59.390 --> 00:31:03.127 line:0%
<i> Like most hummingbirds,
 they have a high metabolism</i>

00:31:03.127 --> 00:31:08.565 line:0%
<i> and need to eat a lot of nectar
 to survive.</i>

00:31:08.565 --> 00:31:12.570 line:0%
<i> These birds have a
 'live fast, die young' policy.</i>

00:31:15.840 --> 00:31:18.742 line:0%
<i> Their long tongues are capable
 of gathering nectar</i>

00:31:18.742 --> 00:31:22.012 line:0%
<i> at a rate of
 20 licks per second.</i>

00:31:22.012 --> 00:31:26.650 line:0%
(buzzing)

00:31:26.650 --> 00:31:30.454 line:0%
<i> Almost as fast as their flying.</i>

00:31:30.454 --> 00:31:31.956 line:0%
<i> Their wings are a blur</i>

00:31:31.956 --> 00:31:35.659 line:0%
<i> as they beat almost
 50 times per second.</i>

00:31:35.659 --> 00:31:37.328 line:0%
<i> With all this activity</i>

00:31:37.328 --> 00:31:42.366 line:0%
<i> their heart rate can exceed
 1,000 beats per minute.</i>

00:31:42.366 --> 00:31:43.834 line:0%
<i> Without the camanchaca,</i>

00:31:43.834 --> 00:31:45.836 line:0%
<i> there's no way there
 would be enough nectar</i>

00:31:45.836 --> 00:31:50.441 line:0%
<i> to fuel these tiny powerhouses.</i>

00:31:50.441 --> 00:31:54.579 line:0%
<i> These are true
 desert opportunists.</i>

00:32:01.085 --> 00:32:02.954 line:0%
<i> The camanchaca's reach
 isn't enough</i>

00:32:02.954 --> 00:32:05.890 line:0%
<i> to sustain animals and plants
 further inland</i>

00:32:05.890 --> 00:32:08.426 line:0%
<i> in Chile's dry interior.</i>

00:32:10.361 --> 00:32:13.064 line:0%
(wind blowing)

00:32:13.064 --> 00:32:18.168 line:0%
<i> In these soils, even bacteria
 struggle to survive.</i>

00:32:18.168 --> 00:32:21.272 line:0%
(thunder)

00:32:21.272 --> 00:32:25.142 line:0%
<i> Despite the odds,
 every so often in the north,</i>

00:32:25.142 --> 00:32:29.079 line:0%
<i> the desert sees an event
 nothing short of a miracle.</i>

00:32:29.079 --> 00:32:33.484 line:0%
(music)

00:32:33.484 --> 00:32:37.821 line:0%
<i> Seeds that have been dormant
 for years erupt into life.</i>

00:32:37.821 --> 00:32:41.292 line:0%
(music)

00:32:41.292 --> 00:32:47.331 line:0%
(music)

00:32:47.331 --> 00:32:49.434 line:0%
<i> Fragile-looking flowers
 fight their way</i>

00:32:49.434 --> 00:32:52.102 line:0%
<i> through the sandy soils.</i>

00:32:52.102 --> 00:32:56.674 line:0%
(music)

00:32:56.674 --> 00:33:00.444 line:0%
<i> The desert is alive
 with a super bloom.</i>

00:33:00.444 --> 00:33:03.914 line:0%
(music)

00:33:03.914 --> 00:33:10.354 line:0%
(music)

00:33:10.354 --> 00:33:17.261 line:0%
(music)

00:33:17.261 --> 00:33:20.130 line:0%
<i> More than 200 species of plants
 spring up</i>

00:33:20.130 --> 00:33:24.502 line:0%
<i> to remind Chile
 of their existence.</i>

00:33:24.502 --> 00:33:27.304 line:0%
<i> This is a triumph
 of resilience.</i>

00:33:27.304 --> 00:33:31.375 line:0%
(music)

00:33:31.375 --> 00:33:37.114 line:0%
(music)

00:33:37.114 --> 00:33:38.782 line:0%
<i> Aside from its beauty,</i>

00:33:38.782 --> 00:33:40.584 line:0%
<i> the flowering desert
 is a banquet</i>

00:33:40.584 --> 00:33:44.254 line:0%
<i> for both beast and beetle.</i>

00:33:44.254 --> 00:33:48.926 line:0%
<i> A surprise windfall for
 the animals of the Atacama.</i>

00:33:51.862 --> 00:33:57.435 line:0%
(peeping)

00:33:57.435 --> 00:34:02.740 line:0%
<i> Elsewhere in the desert, the
 impact of rain feels different.</i>

00:34:07.011 --> 00:34:12.216 line:0%
<i> The soils of the Atacama aren't
 well adapted for holding water.</i>

00:34:12.216 --> 00:34:14.451 line:0%
<i> They quickly become
 overburdened,</i>

00:34:14.451 --> 00:34:15.820 line:0%
<i> triggering landslides</i>

00:34:15.820 --> 00:34:19.023 line:0%
<i> that completely reshape
 the landscape.</i>

00:34:21.658 --> 00:34:27.465 line:0%
<i> For humans, the results
 are catastrophic.</i>

00:34:27.465 --> 00:34:31.568 line:0%
<i> But for nature, these
 landslides are regenerative.</i>

00:34:31.568 --> 00:34:37.674 line:0%
(music)

00:34:37.674 --> 00:34:40.177 line:0%
<i> Nutrients are churned up
 and released,</i>

00:34:40.177 --> 00:34:43.047 line:0%
<i> and life thrives in their wake.</i>

00:34:46.684 --> 00:34:49.620 line:0%
<i> Water that soaks through
 the desert to lowlands</i>

00:34:49.620 --> 00:34:52.256 line:0%
<i> easily carves a path
 through the sand,</i>

00:34:52.256 --> 00:34:54.691 line:0%
<i> creating miniature canyons.</i>

00:34:54.691 --> 00:34:57.127 line:0%
(music)

00:34:57.127 --> 00:35:02.366 line:0%
(music)

00:35:02.366 --> 00:35:04.301 line:0%
<i> Hidden beneath the horizon,</i>

00:35:04.301 --> 00:35:08.872 line:0%
<i> these are ribbons of life
 in a seemingly empty sand pit.</i>

00:35:08.872 --> 00:35:12.476 line:0%
(music)

00:35:12.476 --> 00:35:18.782 line:0%
(music)

00:35:18.782 --> 00:35:22.920 line:0%
<i> Hidden gullies conceal
 a surprising resident.</i>

00:35:25.723 --> 00:35:27.724 line:0%
<i> They might look
 out of place here,</i>

00:35:27.724 --> 00:35:32.463 line:0%
<i> but mountain parakeets thrive
 in the Atacama Desert.</i>

00:35:32.463 --> 00:35:36.968 line:0%
<i> These feathery fluff balls
 make this canyon a metropolis.</i>

00:35:39.503 --> 00:35:41.873 line:0%
<i> They're incredibly social birds</i>

00:35:41.873 --> 00:35:46.209 line:0%
<i> and spend all day together
 in big, friendly groups.</i>

00:35:46.209 --> 00:35:47.811 line:0%
(chirping)

00:35:47.811 --> 00:35:51.648 line:0%
<i> They preen and chatter
 to reinforce strong bonds.</i>

00:35:51.648 --> 00:35:53.383 line:0%
(chirping)

00:35:53.383 --> 00:35:56.987 line:0%
<i> But that doesn't mean
 they don't have BFFs.</i>

00:35:56.987 --> 00:36:00.924 line:0%
(chirping)

00:36:00.924 --> 00:36:03.193 line:0%
<i> The reason behind
 their bright green color</i>

00:36:03.193 --> 00:36:08.232 line:0%
<i> becomes obvious
 when they stop to drink.</i>

00:36:08.232 --> 00:36:10.567 line:0%
<i> The mineral-rich water
 carpets the canyon</i>

00:36:10.567 --> 00:36:13.503 line:0%
<i> in algae and grasses,</i>

00:36:13.503 --> 00:36:16.273 line:0%
<i> camouflaging
 the green parakeets.</i>

00:36:16.273 --> 00:36:19.943 line:0%
<i> And airborne predators
 just fly on by.</i>

00:36:19.943 --> 00:36:23.914 line:0%
(chirping)

00:36:23.914 --> 00:36:27.318 line:0%
<i> These narrow channels
 are a surprising Eden</i>

00:36:27.318 --> 00:36:30.087 line:0%
<i> in a vast wilderness of dirt.</i>

00:36:34.825 --> 00:36:36.594 line:0%
<i> In the south of Chile's
 Atacama Desert,</i>

00:36:36.594 --> 00:36:41.899 line:0%
<i> rains have a more obvious
 effect in the landscape.</i>

00:36:41.899 --> 00:36:43.434 line:0%
<i> In a matter of days,</i>

00:36:43.434 --> 00:36:45.836 line:0%
<i> the dry yellows and browns
 of the desert</i>

00:36:45.836 --> 00:36:48.872 line:0%
<i> are replaced by rich emerald.</i>

00:36:48.872 --> 00:36:53.710 line:0%
(music)

00:36:53.710 --> 00:36:59.416 line:0%
(music)

00:36:59.416 --> 00:37:03.287 line:0%
<i> This unexpected good fortune
 for the animals of the Atacama</i>

00:37:03.287 --> 00:37:06.857 line:0%
<i> attracts visitors
 to the fertile plains.</i>

00:37:11.695 --> 00:37:15.332 line:0%
<i> A South American gray fox
 is here to hunt down a mate</i>

00:37:15.332 --> 00:37:17.702 line:0%
<i> for the first time in his life.</i>

00:37:20.704 --> 00:37:22.939 line:0%
<i> The desert can be
 a lonely place,</i>

00:37:22.939 --> 00:37:26.677 line:0%
<i> and the drive to reproduce
 is all-consuming.</i>

00:37:31.415 --> 00:37:36.620 line:0%
(music)

00:37:36.620 --> 00:37:39.757 line:0%
<i> He might have only one shot
 at finding a mate this season,</i>

00:37:39.757 --> 00:37:43.861 line:0%
<i> so it's important
 to be thorough.</i>

00:37:43.861 --> 00:37:45.496 line:0%
<i> A stranger to this area,</i>

00:37:45.496 --> 00:37:49.100 line:0%
<i> he makes his mark
 on every surface available.</i>

00:37:52.970 --> 00:37:57.674 line:0%
<i> This scent trail is
 the fox's version of a flag.</i>

00:37:57.674 --> 00:38:00.077 line:0%
<i> He's staking a claim
 to the territory,</i>

00:38:00.077 --> 00:38:03.647 line:0%
<i> and access to
 any females in it.</i>

00:38:03.647 --> 00:38:07.517 line:0%
(music)

00:38:07.517 --> 00:38:11.122 line:0%
(sniffing)

00:38:15.092 --> 00:38:18.763 line:0%
<i> It seems he's found a lead
 on a local lady.</i>

00:38:22.199 --> 00:38:23.467 line:0%
(shriek)

00:38:23.467 --> 00:38:25.269 line:0%
(barking)

00:38:25.269 --> 00:38:27.538 line:0%
<i> He lets out a greeting.</i>

00:38:30.407 --> 00:38:33.310 line:0%
(distant shrieking)

00:38:33.310 --> 00:38:38.249 line:0%
<i> Out here, the sound
 travels for miles.</i>

00:38:38.249 --> 00:38:39.884 line:0%
(distant shriek)

00:38:40.484 --> 00:38:41.986 line:0%
(bark)

00:38:43.420 --> 00:38:47.358 line:0%
<i> The female hears him.</i>

00:38:47.358 --> 00:38:52.663 line:0%
<i> Uncertain if he's a threat,
 she's cautious.</i>

00:38:52.663 --> 00:38:54.298 line:0%
(shriek)

00:38:56.767 --> 00:38:59.069 line:0%
(distant shriek)

00:38:59.069 --> 00:39:02.272 line:0%
<i> She provides him
 with a coded message.</i>

00:39:02.272 --> 00:39:06.410 line:0%
(music)

00:39:06.410 --> 00:39:09.813 line:0%
<i> Her urine reveals
 her reproductive status.</i>

00:39:09.813 --> 00:39:12.749 line:0%
<i> It's the beginning
 courtship proceedings.</i>

00:39:12.749 --> 00:39:19.557 line:0%
(music)

00:39:21.091 --> 00:39:26.396 line:0%
(sniffing)

00:39:26.396 --> 00:39:29.366 line:0%
<i> Finally, he tracks her down.</i>

00:39:29.366 --> 00:39:32.336 line:0%
<i> Before he can approach,
 he demonstrates submission,</i>

00:39:32.336 --> 00:39:35.473 line:0%
<i> so she understands
 his intentions.</i>

00:39:40.410 --> 00:39:42.279 line:0%
<i> But he's a little overeager,</i>

00:39:42.279 --> 00:39:44.648 line:0%
<i> and she's not making it easy.</i>

00:39:48.219 --> 00:39:53.390 line:0%
<i> Wrapping her tail around her
 body is her way of denying him.</i>

00:39:53.390 --> 00:39:55.158 line:0%
<i> He'll have to try
 harder than this</i>

00:39:55.158 --> 00:39:57.594 line:0%
<i> if he wants to win her over.</i>

00:39:57.594 --> 00:40:00.030 line:0%
(music)

00:40:00.030 --> 00:40:04.968 line:0%
(music)

00:40:04.968 --> 00:40:10.073 line:0%
<i> It's going to be
 an exhausting few days.</i>

00:40:10.073 --> 00:40:12.376 line:0%
<i> If he forgets
 to pay attention to her,</i>

00:40:12.376 --> 00:40:15.912 line:0%
<i> she has ways of reminding him
 to up his game.</i>

00:40:15.912 --> 00:40:21.318 line:0%
(music)

00:40:21.318 --> 00:40:24.254 line:0%
<i> This pair will remain together
 for five more months</i>

00:40:24.254 --> 00:40:27.291 line:0%
<i> before they go
 their separate ways.</i>

00:40:27.291 --> 00:40:30.794 line:0%
<i> In that time, with any luck,
 they'll leave behind a legacy</i>

00:40:30.794 --> 00:40:34.165 line:0%
<i> in the form of
 up to four offspring.</i>

00:40:36.767 --> 00:40:39.169 line:0%
(shriek)

00:40:39.169 --> 00:40:41.738 line:0%
<i> The rains have provided
 a temporary relief</i>

00:40:41.738 --> 00:40:44.408 line:0%
<i> from desolate dust lands.</i>

00:40:47.110 --> 00:40:49.446 line:0%
<i> But there are many places
 in the Atacama</i>

00:40:49.446 --> 00:40:55.519 line:0%
<i> that have no hope of seeing
 water falling from the sky.</i>

00:40:55.519 --> 00:40:58.755 line:0%
<i> Instead, life here
 has to source moisture</i>

00:40:58.755 --> 00:41:00.657 line:0%
<i> from the ground.</i>

00:41:00.657 --> 00:41:03.661 line:0%
<i> But that's easier
 said than done.</i>

00:41:09.066 --> 00:41:14.104 line:0%
<i> The Salar de Pintados
 is an ancient lakebed.</i>

00:41:14.104 --> 00:41:19.476 line:0%
<i> The soil has extremely high
 concentrations of salt.</i>

00:41:19.476 --> 00:41:22.012 line:0%
<i> It's nearly impossible
 for anything to grow,</i>

00:41:22.012 --> 00:41:23.613 line:0%
<i> much less live.</i>

00:41:23.613 --> 00:41:30.154 line:0%
(music)

00:41:30.154 --> 00:41:32.890 line:0%
<i> Plants that survive here
 have learned to adapt</i>

00:41:32.890 --> 00:41:36.093 line:0%
<i> over thousands of years.</i>

00:41:36.093 --> 00:41:40.397 line:0%
<i> As a result, more than 60% of
 the flora found in the Atacama</i>

00:41:40.397 --> 00:41:43.367 line:0%
<i> is found nowhere else on Earth.</i>

00:41:48.304 --> 00:41:50.240 line:0%
<i> In this dry wasteland,</i>

00:41:50.240 --> 00:41:54.611 line:0%
<i> the tamarugo tree is an island
 of life in a sea of salt.</i>

00:41:54.611 --> 00:41:59.083 line:0%
(music)

00:41:59.083 --> 00:42:02.052 line:0%
<i> A magnet for all manner
 of creatures.</i>

00:42:02.052 --> 00:42:04.554 line:0%
(music)

00:42:04.554 --> 00:42:11.528 line:0%
(music)

00:42:11.528 --> 00:42:15.366 line:0%
<i> In the blazing sun, the inside
 of the tamarugo's canopy</i>

00:42:15.366 --> 00:42:18.002 line:0%
<i> is a sanctuary from the heat.</i>

00:42:21.171 --> 00:42:23.540 line:0%
<i> For ancient nomads
 crossing the desert,</i>

00:42:23.540 --> 00:42:27.811 line:0%
<i> this would have been the only
 natural shelter for miles.</i>

00:42:27.811 --> 00:42:29.346 line:0%
<i> And in the right season,</i>

00:42:29.346 --> 00:42:34.117 line:0%
<i> the tree even bears
 a protein-rich fruit.</i>

00:42:34.117 --> 00:42:39.422 line:0%
<i> The secret of this seemingly
 miracle tree lies underground.</i>

00:42:39.422 --> 00:42:42.793 line:0%
<i> Deep, thick roots
 tap into the water table,</i>

00:42:42.793 --> 00:42:46.363 line:0%
<i> sucking up moisture
 trapped in the earth.</i>

00:42:46.363 --> 00:42:50.100 line:0%
<i> Remnants of rainwater
 filtered from the Andes.</i>

00:42:50.100 --> 00:42:55.205 line:0%
(music)

00:42:55.205 --> 00:43:00.443 line:0%
<i> Remarkably, the tamarugo
 has a modest ancestor.</i>

00:43:00.443 --> 00:43:04.715 line:0%
<i> This is a flowering member
 of the pea family,</i>

00:43:04.715 --> 00:43:07.551 line:0%
<i> an unlikely master
 of the desert.</i>

00:43:17.060 --> 00:43:23.466 line:0%
<i> The Atacama is an unforgiving
 realm of Chilean wilderness.</i>

00:43:23.466 --> 00:43:27.537 line:0%
<i> The desert covers more than
 10% of the entire country.</i>

00:43:27.537 --> 00:43:32.709 line:0%
(music)

00:43:32.709 --> 00:43:35.179 line:0%
<i> Dictating hardships
 for every living creature</i>

00:43:35.179 --> 00:43:38.048 line:0%
<i> that dares to exist
 within its borders.</i>

00:43:38.048 --> 00:43:43.821 line:0%
(music)

00:43:43.821 --> 00:43:49.626 line:0%
<i> The animals of the Atacama
 are enterprising risk-takers,</i>

00:43:49.626 --> 00:43:55.432 line:0%
<i> defending opportunity and
 resources at every turn.</i>

00:43:55.432 --> 00:43:58.168 line:0%
<i> Their lives depend on it.</i>

00:44:00.537 --> 00:44:05.442 line:0%
<i> Only those that dare
 survive Chile's borderlands.</i>

00:44:05.442 --> 00:44:10.514 line:0%
(music)

